- get_context: SplitArrayWidget.get_context is called to render a list of checkboxes with initial data (e.g., `[False, True, False]`). → It creates a single `final_attrs` dictionary to be used for all subwidgets. → It loops through the data, calling `self.widget.get_context` (which is `CheckboxInput.get_context`) for each item, passing the *same* `final_attrs` dictionary instance each time. → When `CheckboxInput.get_context` receives a `True` value, it modifies the passed-in `final_attrs` dictionary by adding `'checked': True`. → For all subsequent iterations of the loop, `CheckboxInput.get_context` receives the `final_attrs` dictionary which now contains `'checked': True`, causing all following checkboxes to be rendered as checked, regardless of their actual value.
